{"agent":"pperf-kilo","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"Given `rollup={\"critical_path_floor_s\": None, \"per_file\": {\"slow_test.py\": 80}}` the `or 0.0` coercion makes `floor <= 0` and the function returns `[]`. A missing floor is an unavailable probe, not a measured zero, so the caller treats “nothing to split” as a pass. The same pattern is in `propose_shard_or_workers`: a rollup with `critical_path_floor_s=100`, `per_file={\"a.py\": 90}` and no `skew` key becomes `skew=0.0`, which is below `prop_shard_skew`, so the result is a `workers` proposal whose `because` says the suite is not skewed when skew was never measured.","digest":"6fafc96e608f7bed","family":"xai","location":"propose_split_files","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"propose_split_files"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The size rule is not applied unless the caller passes `max_file_bytes > 0`. The default is `0`, and that branch skips the size check. Input `rollup={\"critical_path_floor_s\": 10, \"per_file\": {\"tiny.py\": 9}}`, `sizes={\"tiny.py\": 100}`, `max_file_bytes` omitted yields a `split_file` proposal for a 100-byte file. The stated rule is share above the knob and over the size rule; duration alone must not split.","digest":"572b9ab4162814ff","family":"xai","location":"propose_split_files","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"propose_split_files"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"Every kind returns the same string, `propose only: record the change ddflow decision add`. A `split_file` proposal does not name the SZ split command that is supposed to accept it, and shard, worker, and selection proposals likewise do not name the call that performs that change. Required fields are also absent: sample size, effect size, expected seconds saved per run and per day, and risk are not on `Proposal` and are not filled by any generator.","digest":"287a33d4667bfe4a","family":"xai","location":"Proposal.next_call","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"Proposal.next_call"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"Missing or non-numeric misses are not recorded as unavailable. `{\"misses\": None}` (and a missing key) becomes `0` via `or 0`, so ten runs with no miss field and `selected_fraction` present return `None`, i.e. “selection is safe”, when the probe did not run. `{\"misses\": \"unavailable\"}` hits `int(\"unavailable\")` and raises `ValueError` instead of an unavailable result. Narrowing is also unimplemented: runs with `misses=0` and `selected_fraction=1.0` across `prop_select_min_runs` never produce a narrow proposal.","digest":"25c873d33a63c782","family":"xai","location":"propose_selection","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"propose_selection"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"`test_an_unskewed_suite_proposes_a_worker_raise_not_a_shard` and `test_a_skewed_suite_is_a_shard_of_the_slowest_file` both build rollups whose own `skew` is 1.0. For 30/30/40 at 8 workers, `_rollup` sets `critical_path_floor_s = max(40, 100/8) = 40` and `skew = 40/40 = 1.0`; for 90/5/5 it is `90/90 = 1.0`. Both are `>= prop_shard_skew` (0.9). Raising workers cannot beat the 40s file, so the “unskewed” fixture is the shard case, not a worker raise. The two tests demand opposite kinds for the same skew signal, so one assertion is wrong for any implementation that shards when `skew` exceeds the knob.","digest":"8f51bd021d9ab469","family":"xai","location":"tests/test_perf_prop_tests.py:71","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"HIGH","title":"tests/test_perf_prop_tests.py:71"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"`test_a_small_share_is_not_a_split_candidate` does not construct a small critical-path share. With durations 1.0 and 1.0 and `workers=8`, `_rollup` sets `critical_path_floor_s = max(1.0, 2/8) = 1.0`, so `tests/test_a.py` is the entire floor (share 1.0 > `prop_split_share` 0.5) and its size 500 exceeds `max_file_bytes` 100. A splitter that follows “share of the critical path exceeds X and over the size rule” must emit a split; the test expects `[]`.","digest":"235c4da802b6c19e","family":"xai","location":"tests/test_perf_prop_tests.py:52","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_perf_prop_tests.py:52"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":14721,"diff_sha":"528fe8810b0fbc0fe89ff3ea1e8bc19707455aedc67c9ed46e3656cc1d9975db","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/PM-prop-tests","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":68.3,"family":"xai","findings":6,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"0f64f3aed8ddaa0a","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/PM-prop-tests.rubber_duck.grok-4.7.20261110T231929Z-03ba423d.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3],"reviewed_head":"2182ab8cc0593a32c0b724df58e5201b9ae2b7d3","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/config_sections/perf_metrics.py":"100644 df9f4bee3c5cf9df33fbe33834d4b19d92d047cb","ddflow/services/perf/prop_tests.py":"100644 3967b80d8cbfc8f518ff7531d1716e339fe24637","tests/test_perf_prop_tests.py":"100644 123eb485a40a283b33f9ecb72b179b27b5d6b8e7"},"reviewer":"grok-4.7","reviewer_digest":"1857ec352c55ee94","reviewer_families":["google","xai"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["propose_split_files","propose_split_files","Proposal.next_call","propose_selection","tests/test_perf_prop_tests.py:71","tests/test_perf_prop_tests.py:52"],"tree_sha":"2182ab8cc059+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"6 finding(s)"},"id":"eb791e551ed7982262324139e","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":168578,"schema":1,"subject":"PM-prop-tests","ts":"2026-11-10T23:20:38.125262Z"}
